Since Next.js components are isolated, you cannot rely on local state (like `useState` inside the component) to track which tooltip is open. Instead, you will create a Context that lives at the root of your application (or a layout wrapper) and manages the state of the "active" tooltip globally.

Here is the complete implementation strategy.

### 1. Create the Context and Provider

First, create a file (e.g., `contexts/TooltipContext.tsx`). This will hold the state of the currently open tooltip.

```tsx
'use client'; // Required for Next.js App Router

import React, { createContext, useContext, useState, ReactNode } from 'react';

// Define the shape of our context
interface TooltipContextType {
  activeTooltipId: string | null;
  openTooltip: (id: string) => void;
  closeTooltip: () => void;
}

const TooltipContext = createContext<TooltipContextType | undefined>(undefined);

export const TooltipProvider = ({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) => {
  const [activeTooltipId, setActiveTooltipId] = useState<string | null>(null);

  const openTooltip = (id: string) => {
    // If a tooltip is already open, close it first (optional, but good for UX)
    // setActiveTooltipId(id); 
    setActiveTooltipId(id);
  };

  const closeTooltip = () => {
    setActiveTooltipId(null);
  };

  return (
    <TooltipContext.Provider value={{ activeTooltipId, openTooltip, closeTooltip }}>
      {children}
    </TooltipContext.Provider>
  );
};

export const useTooltip = () => {
  const context = useContext(TooltipContext);
  if (!context) {
    throw new Error('useTooltip must be used within a TooltipProvider');
  }
  return context;
};
```

### 2. Wrap Your Application

You must wrap your application in the `TooltipProvider`. In the **App Router**, this is usually done in `layout.tsx` or a wrapper component.

**`app/layout.tsx`** (or a wrapper component):

```tsx
import { TooltipProvider } from '@/contexts/TooltipContext';
import { ReactNode } from 'react';

export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html lang="en">
      <body>
        <TooltipProvider>{children}</TooltipProvider>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

