What are the security concerns when using `postMessage`?

The main security concern with `postMessage` is that it can be used to send messages to any origin, which can lead to security vulnerabilities. To mitigate this, you should always check the `origin` of the message before processing it. For example:

```javascript
window.addEventListener('message', function(event) {
    if (event.origin !== 'https://trusted-origin.com') {
        console.error('Invalid origin:', event.origin);
        return;
    }
    console.log('Received message:', event.data);
});
```

