### Step 1: Create the Project Structure

First, create a folder for your plugin. Inside that folder, create a file named `index.php` (to make it a valid plugin) and a folder named `blocks`.

```text
my-custom-blocks/
├── index.php
└── blocks/
    └── my-custom-block/
        ├── block.json
        ├── edit.js
        ├── index.js
        ├── style.css
        └── save.js
```

### Step 2: Create the Plugin File (`index.php`)

This file registers the plugin with WordPress.

```php
<?php
/**
 * Plugin Name: My Custom Blocks
 * Description: Adds a custom block with Heading, Paragraph, and Image.
 * Version: 1.0.0
 * Author: Your Name
 */

// Register the block
function my_custom_blocks_init() {
    register_block_type( 'my-custom-blocks/my-custom-block' );
}
add_action( 'init', 'my_custom_blocks_init' );
```

### Step 3: Define the Block Schema (`block.json`)

This file tells WordPress what the block looks like, its name, and its attributes.

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://schemas.wp.org/trunk/block.json",
  "apiVersion": 3,
  "name": "my-custom-blocks/my-custom-block",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "title": "Custom Block",
  "category": "design",
  "icon": "image-alt",
  "description": "A block with a heading, paragraph, and image.",
  "supports": {
    "html": false
  },
  "textdomain": "my-custom-blocks",
  "editorScript": "file:./index.js",
  "editorStyle": "file:./style.css",
  "style": "file:./style.css",
  "script": "file:./index.js"
}
```

